# Files whose exact bytes are part of an identity must be byte-identical on every checkout.
#
# A product definition is registered by the sha256 of its file, and a session is pinned to that
# checksum. Git's line-ending conversion on Windows turns LF into CRLF on checkout, which changes
# the bytes and therefore the checksum: the same definition then has one identity on Windows and
# another on Linux, and a database registered on one refuses every session on the other.
#
# These rules keep definitions, seeds, adapter manifests and golden recordings LF everywhere.
products/**/*.yaml text eol=lf
products/**/*.yml text eol=lf
products/**/*.json text eol=lf
apps/web/adapters/**/*.json text eol=lf
